# Euclio — Cline rules

## What this project is
Workflow/heartbeat monitoring SaaS for freelancers: clients → workflows →
ping ingest → watcher opens/resolves incidents → (later) alerts + client-facing
status. Modular monolith: Next.js web service + separate watcher worker,
same repo, deployed as two Railway services sharing one Neon Postgres DB.

## Stack
- Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind 4
- Prisma 7, client generator with output ./generated/prisma
  - enums: import from "@/generated/prisma/enums"
  - Prisma types: import from "@/generated/prisma/client"
- Clerk (auth, DEV instance), Sentry (logging via lib/logger.ts), pg adapter
- Node 22 via nvm (.nvmrc) — shells start on system Node; run `nvm use` before
  any node/npm/prisma command
- Tests: vitest, config in vitest.config.mts (loads .env.local via
  vitest.setup.ts, uses vite-tsconfig-paths). Tests hit the real Neon DB.
- Worker entry: worker/index.ts (node-cron), started with `npm run worker`

## Hard invariants — never violate, flag if a change would
1. Tenant boundary: ownership checks live INSIDE the Prisma query
   (client: { accountId: account.id } in the where clause). Never a
   follow-up JS equality check. Highest-severity review gate.
2. The watcher (worker/watcher.ts) is the ONLY writer of Workflow.status
   healthy/down for heartbeat incidents. Ingest routes only write lastPingAt.
3. The watcher NEVER opens or resolves explicit_fail incidents — those are
   owned by /api/ping/[token]/fail exclusively.
4. Incident rows are never deleted. The nightly purge only NULLs errorText
   (and resets errorRedactedByServer). The fact outlives the data.
5. No PII, tokens, or payloads in logger calls — IDs and counts only.
6. Workflow.status defaults to "pending" on create — never set it in
   create paths.
7. Error text is scrubbed (lib/scrub.ts: truncate-first, then pattern-redact)
   before storage. Never store raw error bodies.

## Conventions
- Server actions pattern: auth() check → redirect if no user →
  getOrCreateAccountForCurrentUser() → ownership-scoped query → mutate →
  logger.info with IDs → revalidatePath("/dashboard").
- Forms: useActionState client components, role="alert" for errors, no toast libs.
- Ping routes: rate-limit → readCappedBody (2KB) → validate → transact.
  GET delegates to POST.
- New env vars go in .env.example with a comment block.
- Schema changes require: edit schema.prisma → npx prisma migrate dev →
  npx prisma generate (client is NOT auto-regenerated; forgetting this
  causes "Invalid value for argument" / "column does not exist" errors).
- Dev and prod share ONE Neon DB. Be careful with destructive commands and
  test cleanup — always scope deleteMany with a where clause, never global.

## Session workflow
- At the start of a task, read SESSION-STATE.md for current milestone state.
  Full history lives in docs/session-history.md — don't read it unless asked.
- Implementation plans live in docs/plans/ (e.g. m3-watcher.md). When
  implementing a milestone, validate each change against its plan.
- When a slice is complete (tests pass, verified), update SESSION-STATE.md:
  move the milestone to done (one line), update open threads and next slice.
- Run `npm test` after changes to worker/ or lib/scrub.ts. Don't claim
  something works without running the relevant check.

## Do NOT build (out of MVP scope unless explicitly asked)
Email/alerting, client-facing pages, billing, multi-user accounts,
anomaly detection. Check SESSION-STATE.md's skip list before adding scope.